@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About</PageTitle>

<h1>About this site</h1>

<p class="lede">
    A capability catalogue for the VellumPdf library, executed in your browser as
    WebAssembly.
</p>

<section>
    <h2>What it does and does not do</h2>

    <p>
        Every document on this site is produced by the real library, compiled to
        WebAssembly and running in this tab. There is no server component. Nothing
        you type reaches one, because there is none to reach, and nothing is
        stored between visits.
    </p>

    <p>
        Sharing is by copying the generated C#, and nothing else. There is no link
        that carries a specification, and no saved state.
    </p>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Versions</h2>

    <p>
        The packages are pinned, so what this site demonstrates is one specific
        release rather than whatever is newest.
    </p>

    <table>
        <caption>Pinned versions</caption>
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th scope="col">Package</th>
                <th scope="col">Version</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td>VellumPdf.Layout</td>
                <td>@LayoutVersion</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>VellumPdf.Conformance</td>
                <td>@ConformanceVersion</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <p>
        <a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/VellumPdf.Layout" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">VellumPdf.Layout on NuGet</a>
        &middot;
        <a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/VellumPdf.Conformance" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">VellumPdf.Conformance on NuGet</a>
